cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Voice Activity Detection for Conversational AI in Clinical
  Simulation-Based Learning: An Empirical Optimisation Framework
message: >-
  If you use this software or methodology in your research,
  please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/herbertkokholm/server-vad-optimisation
abstract: >-
  Open-source implementation of a two-stage methodology for
  optimising server-side Voice Activity Detection (VAD) parameters
  in OpenAI Realtime API deployments. Includes a Central Composite
  Design sweep runner, Response Surface Model fitting, Bayesian
  refinement, Pareto front computation, and publication-quality
  figure generation. Developed in the context of clinical simulation
  training (OSCE) but designed to generalise to any
  server-VAD-configurable speech interface.
keywords:
